#
# The flash profile of the kernel: the board's configuration, less what the
# image in the flash can do without.
#
# The board's own configuration, arch/mips/configs/rtl9602c_defconfig, is the
# complete one. "make linux" builds it and the RAM boots of the bench start it,
# and a RAM boot has no size limit. The kernel in the flash has to fit the
# partition k0, 1359872 bytes, and the complete configuration does not. The
# build system merges this file over that configuration
# (BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CONFIG_FRAGMENT_FILES in the board's defconfig) and kbuild
# resolves the dependencies, so each line below is an option the flash profile
# gives up and nothing else changes.
#
# The product is a transparent GPON ONU. Its bridge, the VLAN translation that
# the switch carries out as flower rules, the PON class with the OMCI device,
# the optics through hwmon and I2C, the watchdog and the root filesystem all
# stay; tests/kernel/required-options.txt lists them, each with its reason.
# What goes is what the product does not use, and what a RAM boot of the
# complete kernel gives when it is needed. docs/handbook/building.rst has the
# measured size of each group and the options that were weighed and kept. The
# build holds the kernel it made to both lists (tests/kernel/check-config): a
# dropped option that kbuild brings back, or a needed one that disappears,
# fails it.

# No symbol table. An oops prints addresses and not function names, and
# /proc/kallsyms is empty. The addresses decode against the System.map of the
# same build, which is reproducible, and the complete kernel keeps the names.
# CONFIG_KALLSYMS is not set

# No IPv6. The management network is IPv4 and the stick has no IPv6 address of
# its own; the bridge forwards IPv6 frames like any other frames.
# CONFIG_IPV6 is not set

# No netfilter. The product neither routes nor translates addresses, so it has
# no flow table to offload, and its filtering is the switch's own, flower rules.
# CONFIG_NETFILTER is not set

# No debugfs and no dynamic debug. They are the views the drivers give a person
# at a console: the PLOAM log, the tables, the decoded readings of the optics.
# The product's own interfaces are the PON netlink family, hwmon and the devlink
# parameters, and a RAM boot of the complete kernel has the views when a person
# needs them.
# CONFIG_DEBUG_FS is not set
# CONFIG_DYNAMIC_DEBUG is not set

# No initial RAM disk. The root filesystem is the SquashFS image in r0, and the
# kernel has no initramfs of its own.
# CONFIG_BLK_DEV_INITRD is not set

# No kexec. A kernel started by kexec does not run on this board, so the system
# call can only cost a power cycle (Documentation/arch/mips/rtl9602c.rst).
# CONFIG_KEXEC is not set
